Keep past principles, on top of it do:
- Covering engineering principles, AI usage rules, and review discipline.
- Changes must be minimal, focused, and justifiable.
- Prioritize readability and maintainability.
- Follow language-specific best practices and coding standards.
- Adhere to existing architectural patterns and separation of concerns.
- Favor simple and optimal solutions over unnecessary complexity.
- Require human validation of all AI-generated code.
- Ensure peer review and constructive feedback before merge.
- Maintain consistency, correctness, security, and long-term maintainability across the codebase.
